    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.nvim' version of \"zenmode\" like functionality is [`MiniMisc.zoom()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f1dd64cf2ac1b348bd440e59446abf680c7188d6/doc/mini-misc.txt#L268-L279). It toggles between showing and unshowing particular buffer \"full screen\". I have it mapped to `<Leader>oz` (\"other\" + \"zoom\") and it works for me quite well.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"already has a version that seems to be enough\".",
